# /etc/sudoers - sudo-rs configuration for the c2s rescue image.
#
# sudo-rs (not the original sudo) parses this file.  Notes that matter for
# this image:
#   * `Defaults !authenticate` is NOT understood by sudo-rs and is rejected
#     as an unknown setting - never add it here.
#   * sudo-rs REQUIRES an active (uncommented) @includedir: without it the
#     rescue account cannot be granted any right.
#   * Password/PAM authentication is not used for granting: both accounts
#     below are NOPASSWD, and dropbear is public-key only (password auth is
#     compiled out of dropbear).  A minimal pam_permit stack in
#     /etc/pam.d/sudo satisfies sudo-rs's mandatory pam_start() call.
#
# The sudoers file and every file in sudoers.d must be owned by root and
# mode 0440, or sudo-rs refuses to load them.
@includedir /etc/sudoers.d
